## Status

Self-excluded: **no verified public benchmark numbers** were found for the exact model/ID `gpt-5.1-codex` in accessible sources at time of research.

## Research notes

- Accessible metadata (not benchmark scores): Artificial Analysis lists GPT-5.1 Codex (High) as a proprietary OpenAI reasoning model (released November 2025, deprecated in AA view), supporting text/image input and text output, with 400k-token context window, knowledge cutoff Sep 30 2024, and pricing around $1.25/$10.00 per 1M tokens (cache discount 90%) in AA snapshots.
- Artificial Analysis reported Intelligence Index and task-level benchmark aggregates as unavailable/N/A in the fetched snapshot. A dedicated OpenAI announcement page for this exact model/ID was not accessible in fetched results (404 on attempted URL), and no extractable standalone verified benchmark scores (e.g. GPQA, SWE-bench, HLE, MMMU, Terminal-Bench, AIME, LiveCodeBench, etc.) for the exact model/ID were found in accessible sources.
- Per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md`: if zero verified public benchmark numbers are found for the exact model/ID, save a notes-only `.md.excluded` file and do not invent placeholder scores.

